## 6. Questions I would value a second opinion on

1. **F-1 severity.** I called it Blocking because it creates a duplicate pending
   artifact and defeats the module's stated idempotency guarantee. It requires
   the stored-receipt-unreadable branch in `_replay`, which is rare. Is Blocking
   right, or is it Important?
2. **F-3 threat model.** Is a hostile or compromised platform server in scope at
   all? Remediation item 3 adopted that model explicitly; if it is in scope, the
   code field must be bounded the same way the message was. If it is not, item 3
   was unnecessary and F-3 is moot. It should not be half-adopted.
3. **F-4 versus the pin invariant.** Scoping the pin check to the requested
   folder would fix the download trap but weakens "only an explicit discard
   clears a pin". Is a separate **Discard Pinned & Download** button the better
   resolution?
4. **F-5 and the pin's durability.** Is an in-memory, per-page-load pin adequate
   for the delivery-indeterminate case, or does the operations guide overstate
   what it protects?
5. Anything in section 3 you think I cleared too readily.

