## 8. Unrelated operational note

During this session the live Discord bot was found down and was restored. It is
recorded here only so you are not misled by host state; **no repository content
was changed** by it, and `git diff --summary` shows no mode changes.

`models/exchange.py` was mode `0600` owned by `foundry`, while the service runs
as `User=discordbot`. `ext/commands/xchange.py:9` imports it, `ext/loader.py`
treats every extension as required, so startup failed with exit code 1 and
`Restart=on-failure` looped it 24,235 times. The file had been unreadable to the
service account since 2026-07-26; the running process held the module in memory,
so the fault only surfaced at the 2026-08-07 11:34 reboot.

Fixed by `chmod`. The same defect — files at `0600` and directories at `2700`,
consistent with a `umask 077` session — was swept from `adapters/`, `domain/`,
`migrations/`, `docs/`, `tests/` and three `application/*.py` files, which
matters because the architecture in `AGENTS.md` has cogs importing from
`domain/` and `adapters/` next. `alembic.ini`, `infra/postgresql/` and
`.pytest_cache/` were deliberately left restricted. `.env` was world-readable and
is now `0640`; **its Discord token and Google service-account key should be
considered exposed and rotation is a maintainer decision.**
